    "body": "## Owner decision recorded: first build is 2 units\n\nThe owner wrote: \"JLCPCB accept at least 2 PCBA, so we\" / \"will make 2 units first\". That answers `assembly:order-quantity`. The 2-board PCBA minimum is **owner-reported**. It could not be confirmed against JLCPCB's published terms from the cloud. The prototype-route decision stays open.\n\n## Scope\n- Record the decision and the owner's sourcing preference (\"basically I want to complete it on JLCPCB, external purchase from JLC parts lib is acceptable\") in a procurement-owned file. The preference order is JLC stock, then JLC pre-order or Global Sourcing, then an exception flagged per line.\n- Add an order plan to the procurement ledger:\n  - Boards: controller 2, led_leaf 4, power_adapter 2.\n  - Per-line pieces for 2 modules.\n  - PCM13SMTR needs 2 pieces against a pre-order minimum of 3, so buy 3.\n  - Attrition is recorded as NOT_SOURCED.\n- Record the 2026-11-12 JLC listing for C221842. Rework the switch-supply decision for JLC pre-order or Global Sourcing. Revisit the material:jack and material:switch requests: loose jacks bought from LCSC are an exception.\n- Let the readiness checklist show answered owner decisions (owner's words plus the record) and remove the closed gate.\n\nThis does not authorize any order, supplier message or manufacturing release. A5 stays immutable.",
